  "content": {
    "id": "p63-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "A sector has the magnitude of its arc length $l$, to the magnitude of its area $A$ in the ratio $2:5$. The sector has area $\\dfrac{15\\pi}{2}\\text{ cm}^2$. Find the angle $\\theta$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p63-q22-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\text{ radians}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p63-q22-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The ratio gives ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "r=5\\text{ cm}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "; substitute into ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "A=\\frac12r^2\\theta",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Using numerical magnitudes with lengths in centimetres and areas in square centimetres,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{l}{A}&=\\frac25\\\\\\frac{l}{A}&=\\frac{r\\theta}{\\frac12r^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{l}{A}&=\\frac2r.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac2r&=\\frac25\\\\r&=5\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $A=\\tfrac12r^2\\theta$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{15\\pi}{2}&=\\frac12(5)^2\\theta\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{3\\pi}{5}\\text{ radians}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
